WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
Billions of people died in Attack on&nbsp;
Titan. Hundreds have been killed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.600
Demon Slayer. But surprisingly only a&nbsp;
mere 80 people have died in One Piece.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.980
So in this video, we will explain every single&nbsp;
character that has been killed in the story.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:20.340
Starting with THE MOST GAME CHANGING DEATH&nbsp;
in the story, the execution of the former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:26.280
pirate king, Gol D. Roger. He was killed&nbsp;
by these World Government executioners,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.080
who can now actually claim the title of&nbsp;
killing the strongest pirate to ever live.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.180
But this monumentous event occurred in the&nbsp;
very first page of the story after Roger had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.820
already found the legendary island Laugh Tale.&nbsp;
But during his journey he became deathly ill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.300
so he decided to turned himself into the&nbsp;
marines. He did this so that he could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.520
inspire the next generation of pirates to find&nbsp;
his legendary treasure and change the world.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.620
However that is far the only death in chapter&nbsp;
1, and it’s kinda crazy that the very first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.820
chapter of one piece is also one of the&nbsp;
bloodiest. Because we also have the death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:08.460
of the captain of the mountain bandits. After&nbsp;
he kidnapped Luffy and clashed with Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.740
he took Luffy out to sea where he was then eaten&nbsp;
by this giant sea monster. And interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:19.860
this is actually the only time we have seen&nbsp;
a named character killed by a sea creature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.080
Kinda weird in a world filled with these&nbsp;
massive monsters. But even before this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.080 --> 00:02:48.840
this random mountain bandit was shot in&nbsp;
the head by Shanks’ crewmate, Lucky Roux.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:10.920
However, after three deaths in the very first&nbsp;
chapter, we have to wait almost two real years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:17.400
until the next death in the story. In chapter&nbsp;
75, we meet the first of many random, unfortunate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:23.940
characters to simply be in the wrong place at&nbsp;
the wrong time. This random marine commodore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.220
who actually has the hilarious name Pudding&nbsp;
Pudding, has come to save Nami’s hometown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.300
from this ruthless group of fishmen. However,&nbsp;
Arlong’s henchmen sink the marine vessel before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:40.200
even landing on the island. This sends sending&nbsp;
Pudding Pudding and his marines to a watery grave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.663 --> 00:03:55.303
killer. And in fact Zoro is next on the list.&nbsp;
Jumping ahead a few more years, and in chapter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.303 --> 00:04:01.663
190 we learned that Zoro killed the former Mr. 7,&nbsp;
a special agent working for the warlod Crocodile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.663 --> 00:04:07.303
sometime before the story began. Apparently&nbsp;
this Mr. 7 tried to forcefully recruit Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.303 --> 00:04:13.843
to Crocodile, but clearly it didn’t end well.&nbsp;
But that’s not even the only one of Crocodile’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.843 --> 00:04:20.623
subordinates to be killed, as Mr. 11 was shot dead&nbsp;
by a supposed ally, Mr. Mellow, in chapter 159.

00:04:20.623 --> 00:04:25.063
Now staying in the sandy wastes of&nbsp;
Alabasta, these guys died by their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.063 --> 00:04:29.323
hand while trying to take down the warlord&nbsp;
Crocodile. These are the Tsumegery Guards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.323 --> 00:04:34.303
and they willingly drank this deadly&nbsp;
Hero Water. Why you might ask? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.303 --> 00:04:40.483
it gives you a ridiculous boost in strength, but&nbsp;
only lasts a few minutes before its effects turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:44.743
deadly for the user. And their sacrifice&nbsp;
just goes to show how truly desperate they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.743 --> 00:04:49.783
were to take down the warlord. And these&nbsp;
are the only official deaths in Alabasta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.783 --> 00:04:54.943
except for any of the random characters who died&nbsp;
in the massive fighting during the civil war.

00:04:56.143 --> 00:05:02.983
And this leads us to the absolute largest named&nbsp;
character to die in One Piece. This giant snake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:06.703
Kashigami, was worshiped by the&nbsp;
ancient people of Jaya. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.703 --> 00:05:11.623
that all changed when the snake god had&nbsp;
it’s head cut off by the explorer Nolan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.623 --> 00:05:17.263
in chapter 287. Nolan did this to save this&nbsp;
woman from being sacrificed. And while this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.263 --> 00:05:22.783
event initially caused much conflict, eventually&nbsp;
Nolan became greats friends with the tribe.

00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:28.123
However, maybe the giant snake was actually&nbsp;
some kind of god, because karma came back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.123 --> 00:05:33.283
bite Noland when he was executed by his own&nbsp;
kingdom. This was because he could not find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.283 --> 00:05:37.423
the famous city of gold a second time . But&nbsp;
this of course was not his fault, since the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.423 --> 00:05:43.783
golden city of Shandora was literally shot into&nbsp;
the sky. But don’t tell that to this greedy king.

00:05:43.783 --> 00:05:51.343
And from one slimy killer to another, let’s&nbsp;
jump ahead six volumes to chapter 356. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.343 --> 00:05:57.643
this chapter, the legendary shipwright Tom was&nbsp;
taken away and supposedly executed by Spandam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.643 --> 00:06:03.403
one of the most hated characters in One Piece.&nbsp;
This was all a set up after Spandam had used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.403 --> 00:06:07.483
young Franky’s weapon to frame Tom. And&nbsp;
so even though it wasn’t Tom’s fault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.483 --> 00:06:11.143
he accepted the punishment to save&nbsp;
his beloved apprentices. But yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.143 --> 00:06:17.563
we really hate this guy. So please Robin, go&nbsp;
ahead, smack him around a bit more for us.

00:06:20.743 --> 00:06:23.263
In fact, if we could wipe&nbsp;
out Spandam’s whole family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.263 --> 00:06:29.443
the one piece world would be a lot better&nbsp;
off. Because Spandam’s father, Spandine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.443 --> 00:06:34.243
was the main government agent who brought&nbsp;
mass destruction to the scholarly island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:45.550
it is nearly not as significant&nbsp;
as the next death on this list.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:53.110
This man right here is Thatch, the second division&nbsp;
commander of the Whitebeard pirates. Or at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.110 --> 00:07:00.430
he was, until he found the darkness logia devil&nbsp;
fruit, and was killed by Marshall D. Teach. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:05.050
at this point, Blackbeard, who was also a part&nbsp;
of Whitebeard’s crew, had been searching for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:10.630
this fruit for twenty-six years. In fact, he&nbsp;
only joined Whitebeard because he thought it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:17.350
was his best chance at finding this one super&nbsp;
special fruit. So Blackbeard literally stabbed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:21.910
Thatch in the back and then left the Whitebeard&nbsp;
pirates for good. And while Thatch himself is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:28.450
not super important, his death kicked off many of&nbsp;
the most important plot lines in the entire story.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.790
Because after Blackbeard betrayed the crew,&nbsp;
Ace set out to hunt down the traitor for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:39.310
revenge. And that all eventually led to Ace’s&nbsp;
capture and the whole war at Marineford. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:44.650
this betrayal won Blackbeard his famous devil&nbsp;
fruit. Which is super game changing because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:50.710
it is literally the most mysterious power and&nbsp;
helped him quickly become an Emperor of the Sea.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:55.930
This takes us to Thriller Bark, where we&nbsp;
met this zombie pirate named Captain John.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.930 --> 00:08:01.090
And while he is already dead when we meet him&nbsp;
— wow that’s an odd statement, but whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:04.930
moving on — we later learned in a question&nbsp;
corner that this former member of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:10.150
Rocks pirates was killed by his own crew&nbsp;
because he refused to share his treasure.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:14.350
And if you think these betrayals are&nbsp;
downright disgusting, then make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:19.870
to keep watching because it is NOTHING&nbsp;
COMPARED TO the next killers on this list.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:26.890
In Sabaody, we meet these inhumanly cruel world&nbsp;
nobles. And in the space of just three chapters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:33.430
we see how truly awful these space-suit wearing&nbsp;
Celestial Dragons are. They needlessly kill not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:40.870
one but two innocent people as if they were bugs.&nbsp;
And while we only see these two particular deaths,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:46.030
we can assume that deaths like this are&nbsp;
common for anyone unfortunate enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:52.270
encounter the Celestial Dragons. Seriously,&nbsp;
these dudes are twisted in all the worst ways.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:59.830
Leaving behind Sabaody, our next death is a big&nbsp;
one, literally. This massive giant, Oars Jr,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:04.930
was a longtime friend of Ace who was taken out&nbsp;
during the war at Marineford. And while it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:11.410
never confirmed that he was dead, he had his&nbsp;
whole leg sliced off by Doflamingo and he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:17.830
bombarded by attacks from countless marines. Plus&nbsp;
we’ve never seen him again in the story, so I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:25.030
assuming that he died, along with lots of other&nbsp;
random marines and pirates during this epic clash.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:32.830
But of course Marineford also gave us THE SINGLE&nbsp;
MOST impactful death for Luffy in the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:38.710
story. That’s because the whole point of the war&nbsp;
at Marineford was to save Luffy’s blood brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:43.810
Ace, who was sentenced to execution by the World&nbsp;
Government after Blackbeard turned him in. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:49.390
while Luffy eventually freed him, the brothers&nbsp;
could not escape the wrath of the marine admiral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:56.770
Akainu, who gave us one of the most soul-crushing&nbsp;
moments in the entire story. This moment broke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.770 --> 00:10:03.670
Luffy. Both physically and mentally. And I can&nbsp;
still remember the deep sadness that I felt seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:09.010
this moment for the first time. And Luffy cannot&nbsp;
process his brother’s death either, and he goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:16.030
into this mindless coma which almost cost him his&nbsp;
life. But eventually this loss made him realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:22.990
that he was not strong enough to protect his&nbsp;
friends, so he decided to train for two years.

00:10:26.002 --> 00:10:29.662
war showed us of the most insanely&nbsp;
overpowered fighters in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:36.502
none of them compare to the single most deadly&nbsp;
force in all of One Piece. That’s right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.502 --> 00:10:44.122
I’m talking about: Stairs. Don’t believe me?&nbsp;
Well, just remember that these stairs easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.122 --> 00:10:51.442
took out Zoro’s childhood friend, Kuina,&nbsp;
who literally defeated Zoro 2001 times. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.442 --> 00:10:57.202
that’s not the definition of a monstrous&nbsp;
force of nature, I don’t know what is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.202 --> 00:11:01.942
And if you want protection from this deadly stair&nbsp;
monster, make sure to subscribe to the channel.

00:11:01.942 --> 00:11:09.982
But after Blackbeard’s complete betrayal&nbsp;
at marineford, we get another example of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.982 --> 00:11:15.382
crew on crew violence during the Ace, Sabo,&nbsp;
Luffy flashback. That’s because this guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.382 --> 00:11:20.422
Porchemy, was killed by his own captain,&nbsp;
Bluejam, for failing to beat up a young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.422 --> 00:11:25.042
Ace and Sabo. Speaking of Bluejam, I don’t&nbsp;
know about you, but I could really go for my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.042 --> 00:11:29.902
own jam sandwich right as we get to the&nbsp;
even deadlier second half of the story.

00:11:29.902 --> 00:11:33.922
And after the two year timeskip,&nbsp;
and a month long break in real life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.922 --> 00:11:41.182
we now move ahead to Fishman Island. In chapter&nbsp;
623 the chadliest of fishman, Fisher Tiger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.182 --> 00:11:46.642
was killed by marines for simply returning&nbsp;
this lost child to her home. And this death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.642 --> 00:11:52.702
meant that fishmen continued to hate humans&nbsp;
for generations. But this hatred had serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.702 --> 00:11:58.102
consequences later on because the human-hating&nbsp;
fishman Hoady Jones actually assassinated the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.102 --> 00:12:03.802
fishmen queen Otohime because of her ideals&nbsp;
about humans and fishmen getting along.

00:12:03.802 --> 00:12:08.542
And soon after the fishman queen’s death, we&nbsp;
learned about the death of THE MOST MYSTERIOUS&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.542 --> 00:12:17.122
CHARACTER in the entire story. When Robin&nbsp;
reads this poneglyph, she learns about Joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.122 --> 00:12:23.182
Boy. The happily named figure was the leader&nbsp;
of the legendary ancient kingdom. While we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.182 --> 00:12:29.362
don’t know exactly what happened, we can assume&nbsp;
that he was killed during the battle with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.362 --> 00:12:33.262
twenty kingdoms. These same twenty kingdoms would&nbsp;
eventually form the World Government. And while we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.262 --> 00:12:38.242
learned a bit more about Joy Boy during the Wano&nbsp;
arc, which I covered in depth in a previous video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.242 --> 00:12:45.262
this is one death we absolutely have to&nbsp;
learn more about before the end of the story.

00:12:45.262 --> 00:12:50.482
But one character we certainly won’t&nbsp;
be hearing from again is Vergo. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.482 --> 00:12:54.022
man was posing as a marine while&nbsp;
actually working undercover for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.022 --> 00:12:58.822
Doflamingo. But after being stuck to the&nbsp;
railing of a laboratory by Trafalgar Law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.822 --> 00:13:04.222
Vergo died in a massive explosion that&nbsp;
rocked the entire laboratory on Punk Hazard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.222 --> 00:13:11.002
so congratulations you food loving man, you are&nbsp;
the first named character to die in the New World.

00:13:13.687 --> 00:13:19.162
But Vergo was quickly joined by this Snow&nbsp;
Logia fruit user, Monet, who was seconds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.162 --> 00:13:23.962
away from blowing up the entire island with an&nbsp;
even bigger explosion. Unfortunately for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.962 --> 00:13:31.282
she was killed when Caesar Clown stabbed her&nbsp;
heart. But little did Caesar know that Law had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.282 --> 00:13:36.742
tricked him, and so he actually killed his own&nbsp;
subordinate instead of the marine admiral Smoker.

00:13:36.742 --> 00:13:40.582
But as hard as it is to watch someone&nbsp;
accidentally kill their friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.582 --> 00:13:47.962
it is nothing compared to the tear-jerking,&nbsp;
sickening sadness of Law’s flashback. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.962 --> 00:13:53.302
we learned that basically Law’s entire&nbsp;
home island, including Law’s sister Lami,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.302 --> 00:13:58.042
were wiped out by neighboring countries because&nbsp;
of a misunderstanding about White Lead Disease.

00:13:59.662 --> 00:14:06.262
Then during chapter 767, this evil young&nbsp;
Doflamingo became so disgusted by his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.262 --> 00:14:10.642
father for taking away their status&nbsp;
as Celestial Dragons. So young Doffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.642 --> 00:14:16.282
shoots Doflamingo Homing himself while his&nbsp;
brother cries in his father’s arms. Damn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.282 --> 00:14:19.942
what a horrible little monster young Doffy was.

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:25.222
And in the very same chapter, we get the&nbsp;
heart-breaking conclusion to Law’s flashback.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.222 --> 00:14:30.922
And here we see Doflamingo’s brother Corazon steal&nbsp;
the Ope-Ope no mi to save Law’s from the deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.922 --> 00:14:35.962
White Lead Disease. He stole the fruit from Diez&nbsp;
Barrels, a pirate who wanted to sell the fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.962 --> 00:14:42.322
to the world government. And this turned out very&nbsp;
poorly for Barrels — I mean how couldn’t it with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.322 --> 00:14:48.622
a name like that. but Doflamingo later killed&nbsp;
Barrels because he wanted the fruit for himself.

00:14:48.622 --> 00:14:53.302
But Doflamingo wasn’t done with his killing&nbsp;
spree yet, because in the same chapter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.962 --> 00:14:59.422
Doflamingo executes his brother Corazon. And&nbsp;
this is honestly one of the saddest moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.422 --> 00:15:04.942
in the story. Corazon fights to stay alive&nbsp;
to hide Law’s frantic cries from Doflamingo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.942 --> 00:15:10.642
and he holds on just long enough&nbsp;
for Law to escape. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.662 --> 00:15:15.082
Law does eventually get his revenge&nbsp;
during the events of the Dressrosa arc.

00:15:15.082 --> 00:15:20.902
But while Doflamingo is our current leading&nbsp;
killer with three, we jump ahead nearly two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.902 --> 00:15:27.502
years to Whole Cake Island, where Big Mom easily&nbsp;
takes the cake as the deadliest individual in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.502 --> 00:15:33.862
One Piece. We learn in a flashback from&nbsp;
chapter 850 that Big Mom killed Zepo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.862 --> 00:15:37.102
the brother of everyone’s favorite&nbsp;
polar bear, Bepo. In that chapter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.102 --> 00:15:42.442
we learned that she stole his entire lifespan as&nbsp;
punishment for trying to steal her Road Poneglyph.

00:15:42.442 --> 00:15:47.122
And the deaths continued at the tea&nbsp;
party, when Katakuri killed this guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.739 --> 00:15:57.099
And then ten chapters after those horrifying&nbsp;
deaths, we get one of the most heroic sacrifices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.099 --> 00:16:03.159
in the story. As the straw hats attempt to escape&nbsp;
from Big Mom and her army, their ship is trapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.159 --> 00:16:09.819
by Perospero’s sticky candy. So this leopard&nbsp;
mink, Pedro, sacrifices himself by blowing up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.819 --> 00:16:15.099
the candy trap with a ton of dynamite. And while&nbsp;
Pedro’s choice did allow the crew to escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.099 --> 00:16:18.639
it was devastating for their emotions. But it was&nbsp;
truly an inspiring scene, so please please Oda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.639 --> 00:16:21.999
don’t ruin it by bringing him back to life.

00:16:23.679 --> 00:16:28.539
And the next death is one that Sanji&nbsp;
would probably be happy to hear. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.539 --> 00:16:35.499
that’s because this lion looking guy who ate the&nbsp;
invisibility devil fruit, Absolam, was killed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.499 --> 00:16:40.059
someone from the Blackbeard Pirates. But it’s&nbsp;
not all good news for Sanji, who desperately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.059 --> 00:16:45.399
wanted the fruit. And that’s becasue Shiryu has&nbsp;
already eaten it and is using it to great effect.

00:16:45.399 --> 00:16:51.639
And this takes us back into Wano, where&nbsp;
we have the most named character deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.639 --> 00:16:57.879
of any arc in the entire story. And it&nbsp;
starts with this smiling little man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.879 --> 00:17:04.119
Yasuie. He was a former daimyo who became&nbsp;
the hero of the leftovers town until he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.119 --> 00:17:09.579
was caught stealing from the Flower Capital.&nbsp;
And this set up his execution in chapter 942,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.579 --> 00:17:13.839
when he reveals his true identity and&nbsp;
gives an inspiring speech to the crowd.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.839 --> 00:17:19.779
This sends the shogun Orochi and his men into&nbsp;
a frenzy and they kill Yasuie immediately.

00:17:19.779 --> 00:17:24.219
But the porcupine haired man is not the&nbsp;
only Daimyo who meets their end during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.219 --> 00:17:29.979
the wano arc. In fact, these three former&nbsp;
Daimyos, Uzuki Tempura, Fugetsu Omusubi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.979 --> 00:17:32.559
and Zoro’s great uncle, Shimotsuki Usihmaru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.559 --> 00:17:37.119
were all killed by Kaido and his crew many&nbsp;
years before the start of the wano arc.

00:17:37.119 --> 00:17:43.659
But it’s not just former samurai on Kaido’s hit&nbsp;
list, as the Emperor even killed one or possibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.659 --> 00:17:49.899
two of his allies. This is Kurozumi Higurashi, the&nbsp;
previous user of the clone fruit. And her partner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.899 --> 00:17:56.199
Kurozumi Semimaru, the previous user of the&nbsp;
barrier fruit. It was confirmed in chapter 972&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.199 --> 00:18:01.419
that Kaido killed Higurashi for interfering with&nbsp;
his fight with Kozuki Oden. And while we don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.419 --> 00:18:06.999
know for sure, we can assume Semimaru also died&nbsp;
around this time since we never see him again.

00:18:09.039 --> 00:18:17.559
And chapter 972 is also the spectacular climax&nbsp;
of Oden’s execution. He heroically survived in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.559 --> 00:18:22.779
a boiling pot of oil for an entire hour.&nbsp;
And because of his super impressive feat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.779 --> 00:18:25.899
Oden’s retainers lived to carry&nbsp;
on his will. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.899 --> 00:18:30.639
Oden himself was basically dead at this&nbsp;
point, and Kaido finished the job with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.639 --> 00:18:36.159
bullet to the head. So in case you’re&nbsp;
keeping track, that’s six for Kaido.

00:18:36.159 --> 00:18:41.079
Then just a single chapter later, Oden’s wife&nbsp;
Toki delivered a chilling prophecy that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.079 --> 00:18:46.419
go on to haunt Orochi for twenty years. However,&nbsp;
the time fruit user was then shot and killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.419 --> 00:18:51.339
by Kaido’s forces, just as she finished her&nbsp;
majestic speech. And I’m just now realizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.339 --> 00:18:56.379
Oda really loves to kill characters right&nbsp;
after they says their truly epic lines.

00:18:57.279 --> 00:19:03.399
And all this takes us to the epic conclusion of&nbsp;
the battle on Onigashima. But before we get there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.399 --> 00:19:08.619
let’s go over some honorable mention killers who&nbsp;
we haven’t yet discussed in the story. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.619 --> 00:19:12.039
we have disease, which wiped out&nbsp;
Brook’s former captain, Yorki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.039 --> 00:19:18.219
and his entire crew. It also claimed the live of&nbsp;
Señor Pink’s child and wife, Gimlet and Russian.

00:19:18.219 --> 00:19:22.839
And it’s at this point, I’d also like to&nbsp;
mention Rocks D. Xebec. The former fleet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.839 --> 00:19:27.279
admiral Sengoku tells us that this legendary&nbsp;
former pirate was killed during the infamous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.279 --> 00:19:31.659
battle of God Valley. And while this may&nbsp;
be true and Rocks could actually be dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.659 --> 00:19:35.199
I find it entirely possible that he may still&nbsp;
be alive somewhere in the one piece world.

00:19:36.099 --> 00:19:45.219
But the greatest honorable mention killer of&nbsp;
all is Oda-sensei himself, who loves to kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:45.219 --> 00:19:51.699
a particular group of characters. And who&nbsp;
might this group of characters be, you ask?

00:19:52.659 --> 00:19:54.579
Anyone in a flashback.

00:19:54.579 --> 00:19:58.899
Well, yes, but no, not that&nbsp;
one. It’s actually: Mothers.

00:19:58.899 --> 00:20:03.519
That’s right. There are almost no&nbsp;
significant mothers still alive in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:03.519 --> 00:20:07.599
the entire story. And that’s because Oda&nbsp;
thinks that if all the mothers were alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.599 --> 00:20:12.999
they would probably stop the kids from&nbsp;
becoming pirates. So Oda usually kills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:12.999 --> 00:20:17.019
them off in some tragic way that leaves&nbsp;
a lasting impression on the children.

00:20:17.019 --> 00:20:22.599
For example, there was Usopp’s mom, Banchina,&nbsp;
who died from illness. Nami’s adoptive mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.599 --> 00:20:27.279
Bellemere, who was killed by Arlong. Robin’s&nbsp;
mom, Nico Olvia, who died in the flames of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.279 --> 00:20:32.619
Ohara. Sanji’s Mom, Vinsmoke Sora, who also died&nbsp;
from illness. Portgas D. Rouge, who died from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.619 --> 00:20:37.946
childbirth while carrying Ace. Rebecca’s mom,&nbsp;
Scarlett, who was killed by Doflamingo’s right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.946 --> 00:20:42.939
hand man, Diamante. And that’s not even including&nbsp;
others we’ve already mentioned like Otohime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.939 --> 00:20:47.559
who was the mother of the mermaid princess,&nbsp;
and Toki, who gave birth to Momo and Hiyori. Or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:59.469 --> 00:21:05.529
have the first of Oden’s Red Scabbards to meet&nbsp;
their end. This is Ashura Doji who was a mountain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.529 --> 00:21:10.629
gang boss until Oden came and tamed the wild lands&nbsp;
of Wano. And after the Scabbards failed to defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.629 --> 00:21:16.089
Kaido, they were confronted by a twisted version&nbsp;
of their former master. Ashura Doji realizes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.089 --> 00:21:21.129
this is another clone created by their former&nbsp;
ally Kanjuro. And with his last act, Ashura Doji&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.129 --> 00:21:25.869
tackles the false Oden and together they fall&nbsp;
into a fiery explosion. And while we’ve seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.869 --> 00:21:32.469
characters survive damage like this before, it was&nbsp;
later confirmed that Ashura Doji did in fact die.

00:21:32.469 --> 00:21:37.569
But speaking of Kanjuro, this traitor died in&nbsp;
a similar blaze of glory. After suffering many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:37.569 --> 00:21:42.309
fatal wounds when battling the Red Scabbard&nbsp;
Kin’emon, Kanjuro crawled back to Orochi’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:42.309 --> 00:21:47.289
feet. Orochi then ordered him to create this&nbsp;
massive blob of hateful flames to consume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:47.289 --> 00:21:53.529
Kaido’s castle and everyone in it. And after&nbsp;
creating this beast, Kanjuro collapsed and die.

00:21:54.069 --> 00:22:00.249
But his master would not survive much longer. Now,&nbsp;
Orochi seemed to die many times during the raid on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:00.249 --> 00:22:05.049
Onigashima, like when Kaido cut off his head, or&nbsp;
when the Scabbards took out many of Orochi’s snake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:05.049 --> 00:22:11.109
heads. However, he always reappeared because of&nbsp;
the special ability of Orochi’s Mythical Zoan:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:12.009 --> 00:22:17.049
Yamata no Orochi devil fruit. This fruit allows&nbsp;
him to have eight lives to go along with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:17.049 --> 00:22:23.109
snake-like eight heads. But by the time we see him&nbsp;
in chapter 1048 he has already had seven of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.109 --> 00:22:29.109
heads already taken out. Orochi is then confronted&nbsp;
by another of the Red Scabbards, Denjiro. And it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.109 --> 00:22:34.389
is fitting that Denjiro is the one to deal the&nbsp;
final blow, because he suffered for years secretly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:34.389 --> 00:22:39.789
plotting Orochi’s downfall for twenty years.&nbsp;
But with a last slash of his sword, Denjiro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.789 --> 00:22:45.429
finally slays the twisted shogun, brining Oden’s&nbsp;
revenge after twenty long years of suffering.

00:22:45.429 --> 00:22:50.709
And good riddance to the most annoyingly&nbsp;
voiced character in the entire anime.

00:22:50.709 --> 00:22:55.929
Unfortunately, there isn’t a completely happy&nbsp;
ending for the Scabbards. With Ashura Doji&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:55.929 --> 00:23:00.489
already dead, the pistol-wielding Izou is battling&nbsp;
against agents of the world government’s CP0.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:01.449 --> 00:23:06.069
Already heavily damaged, Izou clashes with&nbsp;
this guy, Maha, one last time, and the pair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:06.069 --> 00:23:11.949
deal fatal blows to each other. Izou’s death was&nbsp;
later confirmed just like Ashura Doji’s, leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:11.949 --> 00:23:16.809
a bittersweet taste to the end of the war.&nbsp;
But since their famous battle cry Shunnachi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:16.809 --> 00:23:21.489
basically means that they will give THEIR ALL&nbsp;
to achieve victory, I think they will consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:21.489 --> 00:23:27.189
it a sacrifice worth the freedom of their country&nbsp;
after over twenty years of oppression under Kaido.

00:23:27.189 --> 00:23:30.849
But speaking of the big bad man himself,&nbsp;
this brings us to the end of the war on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:30.849 --> 00:23:36.309
Onigashima and the final two deaths&nbsp;
of the arc. Or, umm, possible deaths.

00:23:36.309 --> 00:23:39.969
You see, in chapter 1040, the&nbsp;
tag-team duo of Law and Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:39.969 --> 00:23:44.169
Kid fully unleash their awakened devil&nbsp;
fruit powers to defeat Big Mom. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:44.169 --> 00:23:48.909
Law’s silencing bubble cancels out Big Mom’s&nbsp;
soul powers and then Kid’s super overpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:48.909 --> 00:23:54.969
railgun forces the helpless Big Mom out of the&nbsp;
castle and into a massive hole. And this pit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:54.969 --> 00:23:59.529
leads directly into a pool of volcanic&nbsp;
lava deep beneath the surface of Wano.

00:23:59.529 --> 00:24:03.069
And if that molten lava is&nbsp;
not enough to kill Big Mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:03.069 --> 00:24:07.989
then I truly don’t know if she can&nbsp;
be killed in the story. But for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:07.989 --> 00:24:13.989
we are led to believe that she is dead, since much&nbsp;
time has passed and she still hasn’t reappeared.

00:24:13.989 --> 00:24:16.989
And the same could be said for the&nbsp;
strongest creature in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:16.989 --> 00:24:22.629
Kaido. As the truly epic clash atop the skull dome&nbsp;
came to its end, Kaido used this insanely massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:22.629 --> 00:24:25.646
fire dragon form that towered over the island&nbsp;
itself. As Kaido flew up up into the clouds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:25.646 --> 00:24:28.329
he was met by an even bigger Gear 5 Luffy.&nbsp;
And with this mind-blowingly massive punch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:28.329 --> 00:24:32.949
he crushed Kaido all the way down into&nbsp;
the same underground lava pool as Big Mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:32.949 --> 00:24:38.349
which led to a giant volcanic eruption as&nbsp;
Luffy was declared the victor of the battle.

00:24:38.349 --> 00:24:43.749
And while this was truly an epic moment in the&nbsp;
story, we have to give the same disclaimers for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:43.749 --> 00:24:49.569
Kaido’s death as we did with Big Mom. Kaido might&nbsp;
have somehow survived this titanic explosion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:49.569 --> 00:24:54.249
but for now we are meant to believe that the two&nbsp;
Emperor’s of the Sea are well and truly dead.

00:24:54.249 --> 00:24:59.229
And so after four years in the most&nbsp;
deadly arc to date, the story moved on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:59.229 --> 00:25:05.349
to an even more shocking death, or should&nbsp;
I say, deaths, than anyone could imagine.

00:25:05.349 --> 00:25:11.109
First, in chapter 1054, Nefertari Cobra, who&nbsp;
is the father of Vivi and the king of Alabasta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:11.109 --> 00:25:17.409
was killed during the meeting of the World&nbsp;
Government’s rulers. And this is a truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.409 --> 00:25:21.789
game changing death, since it was blamed on&nbsp;
Luffy’s blood brother Sabo. And while no one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:21.789 --> 00:25:26.769
really believes that it was Sabo, this is hugely&nbsp;
important because not only was Cobra secretly one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:26.769 --> 00:25:33.669
of Luffy’s allies, but he was also one of the few&nbsp;
actual “good” kings in the story. If anyone was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:33.669 --> 00:25:38.829
going to try to change the government for good, it&nbsp;
was going to be him. So with him dead, this means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:38.829 --> 00:25:43.869
that we may be getting an even more sinister world&nbsp;
government that we have had thus far in the story.

00:25:43.869 --> 00:25:50.769
And this leads directly to the destruction of an&nbsp;
ENTIRE ISLAND. In an unthinkable display of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:50.769 --> 00:25:55.929
either the Five Elders, or Imu, the secret ruler&nbsp;
of the World Government, unleashed this massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:55.929 --> 00:26:01.689
blast of laser beams that took out the entire&nbsp;
kingdom of Lulusia. This includes King Seki and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:01.689 --> 00:26:06.669
princess Komane. And this event in chapter 1060&nbsp;
brings to light the truly terrifying powers of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:06.669 --> 00:26:10.389
the world government. They simply decided&nbsp;
that this kingdom was going to be erased,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:10.389 --> 00:26:16.209
and this mysterious weapon of destruction was&nbsp;
able to make it a reality. Now we don’t know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:16.209 --> 00:26:19.869
if this is a devil fruit power or possibly&nbsp;
the ancient weapon Uranus, but either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:19.869 --> 00:26:26.469
this is destruction on a scale WAY BIGGER than&nbsp;
anything we have ever seen in the story. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:26.469 --> 00:26:30.189
makes me wonder if this was how God&nbsp;
Valley was also erased from the map.

00:26:30.189 --> 00:26:32.049
And this takes us to the current story arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:32.049 --> 00:26:37.329
Egghead Island. On this island we are actually&nbsp;
given a genuine murder mystery for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:37.329 --> 00:26:42.969
time in the story. This mystery came to an&nbsp;
epic conclusion in chapter 1077 when Shaka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:42.969 --> 00:26:47.769
the Vegapunk satellite who represents Logic,&nbsp;
was shot in the head by the traitor of Egghead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:47.769 --> 00:26:52.569
Island. And while we don’t truly know&nbsp;
if Shaka is dead, the traitor York,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:52.569 --> 00:26:58.029
who is the Vegapunk satellite representing Greed,&nbsp;
certainly acted like he was out of the picture.

00:26:58.869 --> 00:27:03.549
And just two chapters later, we get&nbsp;
the most undeniably badass one-shot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:03.549 --> 00:27:07.929
K.O. in the entire story, courtesy of&nbsp;
the Yonko Red Haired Shanks. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:07.929 --> 00:27:12.789
with Captain Kid pulled up on Elbaf and was about&nbsp;
to take out Shanks’ entire fleet. However, Shanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:13.509 --> 00:27:18.489
delivers a single godly conqueror’s haki&nbsp;
infused slash that takes out Kid and almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:18.489 --> 00:27:24.549
all of his crew. And then this assault was&nbsp;
followed up by a simply massive dual sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:24.549 --> 00:27:29.829
blast from the giants Dorry and Broggy which&nbsp;
sent Kid and his crew sinking to the bottom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:29.829 --> 00:27:35.589
of the sea. And while we don’t yet know if Kid&nbsp;
will survive this ordeal, the incredible hype&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:35.589 --> 00:27:39.849
surrounding this feat leads me to believe&nbsp;
that he might actually be dead for good.

00:27:39.849 --> 00:27:45.549
And as devastating a blow that will be to Kid fans&nbsp;
everywhere, it is not the first time Kid has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:45.549 --> 00:27:50.649
beaten down. In fact, did you know that he was&nbsp;
actually beaten up by his very first lover? Or did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:50.649 --> 00:27:55.389
you know that Shanks might have been born on God&nbsp;
Valley? Well, if you want to know more about every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:55.389 --> 00:28:01.089
single tragic, epic, and heartwarming backstory&nbsp;
in One Piece, you can watch this video right here.

00:28:01.089 --> 00:28:02.169
Shanks for watching.

